{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2080 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2da8d85ecce828594164f478ef098317940bc4b74318c051a8927f517651f132" :edb/db-before-t 2079 :edb/db-after-t 2080 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535392 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:16:45.362Z" 13194139535392 true] [17592186347065 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347066 13194139535392 false] [17592186347065 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347166 13194139535392 true] [17592186347065 1100 "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,2\\le y\\le 2xz}.\n$$\n\nFor a fixed admissible $x$, let $[a(x),b(x)]$ be the full nonempty $z$ fiber of the exactly specified region $S$. Use ordered inner bounds and the actual outer $x$ range. What is $a(x)\\times b(x)$?" 13194139535392 true] [17592186347065 1100 "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,2\\le y\\le 2xz}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a\\times b?$" 13194139535392 false] [17592186347065 1145 "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=2,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)=2xz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{2}^{2xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}[{\\int }_{2}^{2xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}{\\int }_{2}^{2xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na\\times b=(0)\\times (2x)=0.\n$$" 13194139535392 false] [17592186347065 1145 "The set $S$ is retained exactly. A nonempty $y$ fiber requires $2\\le2xz$, so $xz\\ge1$. The inequality $0\\le z\\le2x$ then forces $x>0$. For a fixed admissible $x$, combine these requirements to obtain\n\n$$\\frac1x\\le z\\le2x.$$\n\nThis interval is nonempty precisely when $1/x\\le2x$, giving $1/\\sqrt2\\le x\\le2$. Every point in this base admits $2\\le y\\le2xz$. Thus the full nonempty $z$ fiber has endpoints $a(x)=1/x$ and $b(x)=2x$, with\n\n$$a(x)b(x)=\\frac1x(2x)=2.$$\n\nThe valid repeated integral is\n\n$$\\iiint_S f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\int_{1/\\sqrt2}^{2}\\int_{1/x}^{2x}\\int_2^{2xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.$$\n\nFor $f=1$, integrating in $y$ and $z$ gives $4x^3-4x+1/x$, hence the volume is\n\n$$[x^4-2x^2+\\ln x]_{1/\\sqrt2}^{2}=\\frac{35}{4}+\\frac32\\ln2>0.$$\n\nThe authentic source solution copied the nominal pair $0,2x$ and reported its product $0$. Its formal repeated integral over $x\\in[-2,2]$ includes reversed and empty fibers; for $f=1$ it gives $0$, not the volume of $S$. The full nonempty fiber has endpoint product $2$." 13194139535392 true] [17592186347166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347067 13194139535392 true] [17592186347166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347068 13194139535392 true] [17592186347166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347069 13194139535392 true] [17592186347166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347070 13194139535392 true] [17592186347166 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347071 13194139535392 true] [17592186347166 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535392 true] [17592186347166 1041 "selection" 13194139535392 true] [17592186347166 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347068 13194139535392 true] [17592186347166 1110 #uuid "af8fc409-93f1-5b75-8606-5962e97972e4" 13194139535392 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-161729/nonempty-fibers-v1/selection" 17592186347166}}
